# Design System Playbook — required reading

Before implementing, refactoring, or auditing any UI in `src/`, you MUST read:

**`docs/design/PLAYBOOK.md`**

The playbook is the operational layer of the design system — the mandatory workflow, anti-patterns, and self-audit checklist for building UI in this repo. Each rule exists because something went wrong once. **Do not re-debate rules already in the playbook** — implement according to the playbook. The spec it points to (tokens, foundations, patterns, motion, states, voice) lives in the other `docs/design/` documents.

## What the playbook covers

1. **Component canonical sources** — when to use `<Button>` primary vs ghost vs destructive, when to use `<Modal>` vs `<Sheet>`, when `<Combobox>` vs `<MultiTagAutocomplete>`, etc.
2. **Token conventions** — `--border` vs `--border-strong`, `--text-on-accent` light vs dark, status enum tokens, layout magic numbers.
3. **Canonical patterns by scenario** — confirm modal destructive, autocomplete with tags, filter chips display, section card disabled-gated, field-as-attribute, toast neutral-undo.
4. **Anti-patterns explicit** — no `<select>` HTML native, no Portal+div modals, no hardcoded `text-white`, no hardcoded literals, no inventing variants without ADR.
5. **Mandatory workflow before implementing UI** — read playbook, demo HTML, component spec, ADRs, tokens.
6. **Self-audit checklist before closing** — TodoWrite, visual verification vs demo, comparative audit, validation, snippet-in-report.
7. **Cross-cutting handling during a session** — flag instead of silent fix.
8. **What to update when a module closes** — playbook, lessons-learned, cross-cutting registry, ADR.

