## Reinforcing rules also `alwaysApply: true`

- `coding-standards.mdc` — base coding behavior.
- `english-code-only.mdc` — code in English, copy in i18n.
- `validation-checklist.mdc` — final validation commands.
- `theme-light-dark.mdc` — both themes are first-class.
- `modal-canonical-pattern.mdc` — Modal canonical component (this rule's sibling for Modal specifically).

## When this rule applies

- Any creation, refactor, or audit of UI components in `src/components/`.
- Any creation, refactor, or audit of pages in `src/app/`.
- Any work on the demo HTML in `docs/redesign/_notes/demo-screens.html`.
- Any audit of a screen against the demo.

## Skip if

- Pure data-layer / Prisma / server-action changes with zero UI touch.
- Pure documentation work in `docs/product/` (FRDs, etc.) without code consequences.
- Test infrastructure that does not render UI.

For everything else: read the playbook first.
